---
import { SITE, ANALYTICS } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// privacy 页关于统计的那一段，必须和站上实际装的东西一致。
// 判断依据是 consts.ts 里的 token —— 填了就描述统计，没填就说没有。
// 这样不会出现「页面声称有统计、实际没装」这类前后矛盾。
const analyticsOn = ANALYTICS.cfBeaconToken.trim().length > 0;
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, what it doesn't, and how third-party affiliate tracking works."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Short version: no accounts, no personal data collected, nothing sold. Affiliate links are covered below, along with exactly what this site does and does not measure.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    This is a static site. There are no accounts, no comments, and no forms. <strong>The site itself collects nothing that identifies you.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    The host (Cloudflare) keeps standard server logs for security and operations, which can include IP address, browser type, and request time. Those logs belong to the host; I only see aggregate figures.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  {
    analyticsOn ? (
      <>
        <p>
          This site uses cookie-free analytics that do not track you across
          sites. It records page views, referring domain, and approximate
          region.{' '}
          <strong>No tracking cookies, no profiles, no cross-site tracking.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="meta">
          The provider is Cloudflare Web Analytics. Measurements stay
          aggregate; they are not used to build a profile of you.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <p>
          <strong>This site currently runs no analytics at all.</strong> No
          page-view counter, no visitor IDs, no third-party measurement
          scripts.{' '}
          <em>
            (Server logs kept by the host, described above, are the only
            record that a visit happened.)
          </em>
        </p>
        <p class="meta">
          If that changes, this section will say so before the change goes
          live.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }
  <p class="meta">
    <!-- 装统计时：把 src/consts.ts 里 ANALYTICS.cfBeaconToken 填上，
         上面这段会自动切换成「使用无 cookie 统计」的版本，不用手改这里。
         若改用 Google Analytics：GA 会设置 cookie、跨站跟踪，GDPR 地区需要
         同意横幅——那时必须重写这一段，不要直接沿用。 -->
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links and third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site carries no affiliate links at present. If it does in future, clicking one may cause <strong>the destination merchant or affiliate network to set a cookie in your browser</strong> so that a later purchase can be attributed here and a commission paid to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those cookies are set and read by third parties. This site can't see inside them and can't delete them on your behalf. You can:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>block third-party cookies in your browser settings;</li>
    <li>visit the merchant in a private window;</li>
    <li>skip the link entirely and search for the merchant by name — the price is identical.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The full explanation is in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    This site links out to third-party websites. Once you leave, their privacy policies apply; I'm not responsible for their content or how they handle data.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because this site stores no personal data about you, there's usually nothing to access, correct, or delete. If you believe it holds information about you in some way, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email me</a> and I'll check and deal with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date below changes when this policy does. Anything that materially changes how data is handled will also be noted on the home page.
  </p>

  <p class="meta">Last updated: October 2026</p>
</Base>
